<http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "License"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A legal document giving official permission to do something with the resource."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/rights> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/LicenseDocument> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/mediator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/mediator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mediator"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/mediator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An entity that mediates access to the resource and for whom the resource is intended or useful."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/mediator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In an educational context, a mediator might be a parent, teacher, teaching assistant, or care-giver."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/mediator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/audience> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/mediator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/AgentClass> .
