<http://purl.org/dc/terms/AgentClass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A group of agents."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/AgentClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Examples of Agent Class include groups seen as classes, such as students, women, charities, lecturers."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/BibliographicResource> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/BibliographicResource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bibliographic Resource"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/BibliographicResource> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A book, article, or other documentary resource."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/FileFormat> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/FileFormat> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "File Format"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/FileFormat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A digital resource format."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/FileFormat> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Examples include the formats defined by the list of Internet Media Types."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/FileFormat> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/MediaType> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Frequency> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Frequency> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Frequency"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Frequency> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A rate at which something recurs."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Jurisdiction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Jurisdiction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Jurisdiction"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Jurisdiction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The extent or range of judicial, law enforcement, or other authority."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Jurisdiction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/LocationPeriodOrJurisdiction> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/LicenseDocument> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/LicenseDocument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "License Document"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/LicenseDocument> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A legal document giving official permission to do something with a Resource."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/LicenseDocument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/RightsStatement> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/LinguisticSystem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/LinguisticSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Linguistic System"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/LinguisticSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A system of signs, symbols, sounds, gestures, or rules used in communication."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/LinguisticSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Examples include written, spoken, sign, and computer languages."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Location> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Location> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Location"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Location> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A spatial region or named place."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Location> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/LocationPeriodOrJurisdiction> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/LocationPeriodOrJurisdiction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/LocationPeriodOrJurisdiction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Location, Period, or Jurisdiction"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/LocationPeriodOrJurisdiction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A location, period of time, or jurisdiction."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MediaType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MediaType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Media Type"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MediaType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A file format or physical medium."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MediaType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/MediaTypeOrExtent> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MediaTypeOrExtent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MediaTypeOrExtent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Media Type or Extent"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MediaTypeOrExtent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A media type or extent."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MethodOfAccrual> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MethodOfAccrual> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Method of Accrual"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MethodOfAccrual> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A method by which resources are added to a collection."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MethodOfInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MethodOfInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Method of Instruction"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/MethodOfInstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process that is used to engender knowledge, attitudes, and skills."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Period of Time"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An interval of time that is named or defined by its start and end dates."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PeriodOfTime> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/LocationPeriodOrJurisdiction> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PhysicalMedium> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PhysicalMedium> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Physical Medium"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PhysicalMedium> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A physical material or carrier."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PhysicalMedium> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Examples include paper, canvas, or DVD."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PhysicalMedium> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/MediaType> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PhysicalResource> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PhysicalResource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Physical Resource"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/PhysicalResource> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material thing."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Policy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Policy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Policy"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Policy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A plan or course of action by an authority, intended to influence and determine decisions, actions, and other matters."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/ProvenanceStatement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/ProvenanceStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Provenance Statement"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/ProvenanceStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A statement of any changes in ownership and custody of a resource since its creation that are significant for its authenticity, integrity, and interpretation."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/RightsStatement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/RightsStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rights Statement"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/RightsStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A statement about the intellectual property rights (IPR) held in or over a Resource, a legal document giving official permission to do something with a resource, or a statement about access rights."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/SizeOrDuration> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/SizeOrDuration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Size or Duration"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/SizeOrDuration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A dimension or extent, or a time taken to play or execute."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/SizeOrDuration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Examples include a number of pages, a specification of length, width, and breadth, or a period in hours, minutes, and seconds."@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/SizeOrDuration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/MediaTypeOrExtent> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Standard> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Standard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Standard"@en-us .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/Standard> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A basis for comparison; a reference point against which other things can be evaluated."@en-us .
